    "problem_statement": "# Sorting tables doesn't work properly\n\nI'm trying to sort tables in my code but it's not working as expected. When I try to sort a table, I get an `UnboundLocalError` exception.\n\nHere's a simple reproduction script:\n\n```python\nfrom textfsm import texttable\n\n# Create a simple table\ntable = texttable.TextTable()\ntable.header = ('Col1', 'Col2', 'Col3')\ntable.Append(('lorem', 'ipsum', 'dolor'))\ntable.Append(('ut', 'enim', 'ad'))\ntable.Append(('duis', 'aute', 'irure'))\n\n# Try to sort the table\ntable.sort()  # This fails with UnboundLocalError\n```\n\nWhen running this code, I get:\n```\nUnboundLocalError: local variable 'result' referenced before assignment\n```\n\nThis happens with both the default sort and when using custom key functions. I'm using the latest version of textfsm.\n\nHas anyone else encountered this issue? It seems like the sorting functionality is completely broken."
